                                "sense_id": "a71efd6e-d28f-3483-b8e2-91137d6a8fd9",
                                "text": "Indeed Belmont, though more classic, owes much to this hip-roofed, belvedered house type."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b0525b4c-32ec-400a-b094-bea5f632f752",
                                "sense_id": "a71efd6e-d28f-3483-b8e2-91137d6a8fd9",
                                "text": "... for the rest of the town, a pleasant confusion of green tree-tops, red and gray roofs, and glimpses of white or yellow wall, spreading back a few hundred yards behind the cathedral, and tapering into a single rank of gardened and belvedered villas, that studded either horn of the river's crescent with a style of home than which there is probably nothing in the world more maternally home-like"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "59326ba4-1e4e-44f7-9435-57759a622298",
                                "sense_id": "a71efd6e-d28f-3483-b8e2-91137d6a8fd9",
                                "text": "Our progress was slow when we came at last to the belvedered plantation houses amongst the orange groves; and as we sat on the wide galleries in the summer nights, we heard all the latest gossip of the capital of Louisiana."
                            }
